A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate when the evidence supports the **same cause** as an open ticket
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), replacing decision 0001):

1. preserve its ID, body, receipt time, and merge history;
2. look up the tenant's locale and booking form, then inspect the channel and symptoms;
3. merge only into a ticket with a confirmed matching cause; otherwise keep it separate.

<Callout>
Subject lines help find candidates. They do not prove that two reports have the same cause.
Keep the parser and booking-v3 hint problems in separate tickets.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report separate and investigate. Unknown tenants and one-day anomalies need
more evidence; do not silently absorb them into a known issue.
